    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine today is headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (75.38) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs near or above 4.70. **Kyle Tucker** remains our most reliable asset, with the algorithm ignoring his lower lineup placement to highlight his elite base production against Nick Martinez. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is a high-upside play against the struggling Spence; the combination of the #2 lineup spot and a significant 14% dynamic platoon advantage makes him a cornerstone of today's production. **Curtis Mead** (63.58) and **Josh Jung** (65.53) also project as strong starts, as both capitalize on the favorable matchup against Spence and Paredes, respectively, with double-digit SP skill bonuses pushing their efficiency scores into the \"Strong\" tier.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved balancing the speed-first profile of **Cole Carrigg** (55.71) against the solid, if unspectacular, floor of **Wade Meckler** (58.29). While **Cole Carrigg** offers the switch-hitting versatility and stolen base potential we prioritize, the risk of facing a top-tier arm in Imanaga kept his score just below our preferred threshold. **Jacob Wilson** (58.75) also sits in the marginal tier; while he benefits from a park-factor boost, facing a competent arm in Jones limits his overall ceiling. We are currently monitoring the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, whose IL stints continue to pinch our depth, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining healthy core. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** currently unavailable due to scheduling gaps, we must extract maximum value from **Liam Hicks** at the top of the order, despite the stiff test presented by Wheeler.",
